# Every file checks out with LF, on every platform. Nothing here needs CRLF, and
# a Windows checkout that rewrote line endings would fail every test that
# compares a file byte for byte - a golden file, a config fixture - over how the
# working copy spells a line break rather than over what the file records.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden files are data. Not converting them at all is stronger than converting
# them to LF: whatever bytes they record are the bytes the test compares.
*.golden -text

# The same, said outright for the media the tests decode. text=auto would leave
# these alone on its own, by noticing they are binary - saying so is not relying
# on it noticing.
*.webp binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
